# Project text files — upkeep

**Project text files** = all `.md` and `.txt` in the repo (README.md, documentation/**/*.md, design-system/**/*.md, TODO.txt, etc.). When you change code or any of these files, update the others in the **same change set**. Do not leave them stale or inconsistent with each other.

## Which text file(s) to update

| You changed | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| Product scope, features, or flows | **documentation/REBUILD.md** (Product, Key flows, DOM, State). |
| Init order, auth, realtime, or data flow | **documentation/REBUILD.md** + **documentation/architecture.md**. |
| New or renamed function | **documentation/functions-index.md** + **documentation/CODE-REFERENCE.md** (Functions). |
| New or renamed variable or constant | **documentation/CODE-REFERENCE.md** (Constants or Variables). |
| DOM elements, IDs, global state, or who sets them | **documentation/REBUILD.md** + **documentation/ELEMENTS.md**. |
| CSS variables, breakpoints, or body/class states | **documentation/REBUILD.md** (Styling) + **documentation/styling.md**. |
| Layout, components, or UI structure | **design-system/components.md**. |
| Modes (select, edit, DnD, view, modals) | **design-system/modes.md**. |
| Animations or DnD tokens | **design-system/animations.md** (+ **design-system/dnd.md** if DnD behavior). |
| Colors or typography tokens/copy | **design-system/colors.md**, **design-system/text.md**. |
| RLS, channel_members, or access rules | **documentation/REBUILD.md** (Security) + **documentation/security.md** (and SQL if needed). |
| Gotcha, convention, or "don't do X" | **documentation/REBUILD.md** (Edge cases) + **documentation/edge-cases.md**. |
| File layout or entry point | **documentation/REBUILD.md** (File layout) + **README.md** (File layout). |
| Backlog, roadmap, or tech debt | **TODO.txt** (and **documentation/DIRECTION.md** or **documentation/OPTIMIZATION.md** if relevant). |
| Doc index or where to find things | **documentation/README.md**; root **README.md** if entry points or layout changed. |

## Rules

1. **All text files are part of the project.** Treat every `.md` and `.txt` as live: accurate and consistent with code and with each other.
2. **REBUILD.md is the single rebuild source.** Keep it accurate; other docs can be longer; REBUILD stays terse with pointers.
3. **One change set.** Edit the affected text file(s) in the same commit/PR as the code or content change.
4. **design-system/** defines UI/UX tokens and behavior; code and REBUILD follow it.
5. **When editing a text file:** if your edit contradicts code or another text file, fix the code or the other file in the same change set so everything matches.

After any non-trivial code or config change, check the table and update the listed text files. When editing any .md or .txt, ensure it stays consistent with the rest of the project.
